      "text_in_image": [
        "SECTION 01",
        "Why 5SMA?",
        "As a swing trader, speed is everything. You cannot afford to be late in reading the market - especially during bear market rallies where conditions can reverse sharply and without warning. The 5-period Simple Moving Average (5SMA) gives you an immediate, no-lag read on basic market health. It cuts through the noise and tells you right now whether the market is in a favourable or unfavourable state for your trades.",
        "Speed matters. The 5SMA is your fastest honest signal of market health.",
        "Why Not Use It on a Daily Chart?",
        "Using the 5SMA on a daily timeframe produces a sluggish, near-useless signal. The correct timeframe is the 25-minute chart. Here is the math behind it:",
        "Indian Market Hours 375 minutes per day",
        "Preferred Candle Size 25 minutes",
        "Candles per Day 375 / 25 = 15 candles",
        "5SMA on 25-min equals ~75 SMA on the Daily chart",
        "Do NOT apply this on the Daily chart. The signal becomes too slow and defeats the purpose."
      ],
      "annotated_levels": [],
      "non_chart_evidence": [],
      "structure_note": "Document page explaining why 5SMA on a 25-minute timeframe is used for market health tracking.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "unreadable": false
