        "SECTION 03",
        "Structure Change with Respect to 5SMA",
        "Here is the crucial filter that separates real signals from false ones. A raw reclaim or breakdown of the 5SMA is not enough on its own. You need to see a structure change in price action - either just before or just after the 5SMA cross. Without this confirmation, you are chasing noise.",
        "What Does a Structure Change Look Like?",
        "Before the index reclaims or breaks the 5SMA, you will almost always see the market form a base - a period of consolidation where price stops making new lows (or highs) and begins to tighten. This is typically a VCP: Volatility Contraction Pattern."
      ],
      "annotated_levels": [],
      "non_chart_evidence": [],
      "structure_note": "Document page explaining structure change with respect to 5SMA and Volatility Contraction Pattern (VCP) confirmation.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
